1
00:04:53,076 --> 00:04:59,076
Everyone deserves a second shot.

2
00:09:46,153 --> 00:09:52,153
Thunderbolts* is a action, science fiction,
adventure film directed by Jake Schreier.

3
00:14:39,230 --> 00:14:45,230
After finding themselves ensnared in a death trap, seven disillusioned castoffs must embark on a
dangerous mission that will force them to confront the darkest corners of their pasts.

4
00:19:32,307 --> 00:19:38,307
Yelena Belova, played by Florence Pugh.

5
00:24:25,384 --> 00:24:31,384
Bucky Barnes, played by Sebastian Stan.

6
00:29:18,461 --> 00:29:24,461
Valentina Allegra de Fontaine, played by Julia Louis-Dreyfus.

7
00:34:11,538 --> 00:34:17,538
Robert Reynolds, played by Lewis Pullman.

8
00:39:04,615 --> 00:39:10,615
Alexei Shostakov, played by David Harbour.

9
00:43:57,692 --> 00:44:03,692
John Walker, played by Wyatt Russell.

10
00:48:50,769 --> 00:48:56,769
Thunderbolts*  is a 2025 American superhero film based on
Marvel Comics featuring the team Thunderbolts.

11
00:53:43,846 --> 00:53:49,846
Produced by Marvel Studios and distributed by Walt Disney Studios Motion
Pictures, it is the 36th film in the Marvel Cinematic Universe (MCU).

12
00:58:36,923 --> 00:58:42,923
The film was directed by Jake Schreier from a screenplay by Eric Pearson and Joanna Calo, and stars an ensemble cast featuring Florence Pugh, Sebastian Stan, Wyatt
Russell, Olga Kurylenko, Lewis Pullman, Geraldine Viswanathan, Chris Bauer, Wendell Pierce, David Harbour, Hannah John-Kamen, and Julia Louis-Dreyfus.

13
01:03:30,000 --> 01:03:36,000
In the film, a group of antiheroes are caught in a deadly trap and
forced to work together on a dangerous mission.

14
01:08:23,076 --> 01:08:29,076
Marvel Studios first teased the formation of an MCU Thunderbolts team in 2021.

15
01:13:16,153 --> 01:13:22,153
The film was revealed to be in development in June 2022,
when Schreier and Pearson were attached.

16
01:18:09,230 --> 01:18:15,230
The main cast was revealed in September, with
additional casting through early 2023.

17
01:23:02,307 --> 01:23:08,307
Lee Sung Jin joined to rewrite the script by March 2023, one of several creatives who
returned to work with Schreier from the Netflix series Beef (2023–present).

18
01:27:55,384 --> 01:28:01,384
Production was delayed by the 2023 Hollywood labor
disputes, causing some cast changes in early 2024.

19
01:32:48,461 --> 01:32:54,461
Calo joined by then for further rewrites.

20
01:37:41,538 --> 01:37:47,538
Filming took place from February to June 2024 at Trilith Studios and Atlanta Metro
Studios in Atlanta, Georgia, and on location in Utah and Kuala Lumpur.

21
01:42:34,615 --> 01:42:40,615
Thunderbolts* premiered on April 22, 2025, at the Cineworld Leicester Square in London, England, and
was released in the United States on May 2 as the final film of Phase Five of the MCU.

22
01:47:27,692 --> 01:47:33,692
The asterisk in the title was the subject of commentary during the film's marketing campaign, and was explained by the reveal at the end of the film that the
Thunderbolts team is rebranded as the "New Avengers"; the title is changed to The New Avengers during the film's end credits and in some post-release marketing.

23
01:52:20,769 --> 01:52:26,769
The film received generally positive reviews from critics, but
underperformed at the box office, grossing $382 million.

24
01:57:13,846 --> 01:57:19,846
The film explores themes of new york city, superhero,
villain, based on comic, super power.

25
02:02:06,923 --> 02:02:12,923
The tone is dark and thought_provoking.
